            <ArticleTitle>Leiomyosarcoma of the ovarian vein: an unusual cause of severe abdominal and flank pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>234-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Leiomyosarcoma arising from the ovarian vein is extremely rare: only one case was found in the literature. We report a case in a sixty-one-year-old woman who had unexplained attacks of pain in her left lower abdomen and flank for two years.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
